**Nucleolar 5-EU mean intensity, Cisplatin 10 µM versus Untreated.**

[Cell line] cells were treated as indicated ([treatment and duration]) and imaged ([antibody or dye for each stain]). Small dots show individual nucleoli, coloured by run; large symbols show the value of each run (median of observations per field → mean of fields per sample → mean of samples per run); lines join the same run; horizontal lines show the mean of runs. n = 3 runs per condition; 281 nucleoli (Untreated) and 207 nucleoli (Cisplatin 10 µM) from 9 (Untreated) and 9 (Cisplatin 10 µM) fields. Nucleoli and fields are not independent replicates. Per-run change of Cisplatin 10 µM relative to Untreated: Rep1 +132%, Rep2 −3.6%, Rep3 −11%. Descriptive comparison: run independence was not confirmed, so no hypothesis test or confidence interval was calculated.
